  "scope": "Add an internal exact-cutoff current-calendar composition, generic cutoff-aware current runtime reads, and an optional timezone-map definition. This is not the calendar evidence adapter or source-closure exit.",
  "implementation": [
    "Omitted/None as_of preserves the old getter path. Explicit aware cutoff reads one current profile, matching snapshot and exact persisted values once; no historical fallback.",
    "Environment, ACTIVE status, profile/snapshot id/key/version, full-profile hash, actual public projection equality and snapshot public hash must agree.",
    "Profile created_at/activated_at and snapshot generated_at/effective_from must be real aware datetimes no later than cutoff; activation equals effective time. No new ordering rule between other clocks.",
    "Optional non-secret NORMAL typed JSON definition uses the existing initialize_runtime_definitions/profile management; no default, seed, migration, production activation or required legacy market field.",
    "New internal calendar entry forwards the same typed query/cutoff to the existing use case, real repository and Core Audit bridge in one default-alias outer transaction; old HTTP/current behavior remains.",
    "Two existing current-data contracts extended without removing tests/markers; optional runtime definition registered against the actual generic getter. Official module map regenerated and byte-identical."
  ],
